# Site secrets. This file does NOT belong in the image and does NOT belong in git.
#
# Copy it onto the BOOT MEDIUM as `polyptic/site.conf`, alongside `polyptic/wifi.conf`. That is the
# same place, and the same trust model, as the Wi-Fi credentials: readable by anyone holding the USB
# stick, and never published anywhere. On a box that has been installed to its own disk the medium is
# that box's EFI system partition, so one mechanism covers both kinds of box.
#
# WHY NOT IN THE IMAGE. `rootfs.squashfs` is served without authentication, because a box has no
# session before it boots and the boot chain cannot present one. Anyone who can reach the control plane
# can download the image and unpack it. A token baked into it is a published token.
#
# FORMAT. One `SITE_<NAME>=<value>` per line. Names are A-Z, 0-9 and underscore. The value is taken
# verbatim from the first `=` to the end of the line, so spaces, quotes, `=` and `$` all need no
# escaping and cannot execute anything: this file is parsed, never sourced. `#` starts a comment. A key
# with an empty value counts as unset, so a template can ship blank keys. The first occurrence of a key
# wins.
#
# A key without the SITE_ prefix is a hard error rather than a silent skip. A typo'd credential that is
# quietly ignored gives you a box that boots, renders perfectly and is enrolled in nothing, which
# nobody notices until an audit.
#
# These reach your firstboot.d/ hooks as environment variables and as files under
# $POLYPTIC_SITE_SECRETS_DIR.

# SITE_EXAMPLE_TENANT=
# SITE_EXAMPLE_ENROL_TOKEN=
